Subject: [PATCH] DIAG ONLY: panic at the end of kernel init to prove liveness

Diagnostic scaffold, not part of the KVM feature work and not to be left
enabled in a "real" build.

The custom kernel boots past the secure world and then appears to hang at the
Motorola logo: no adb, no fastboot, no reboot loop, no sysdump.  A second
hypothesis fits the same symptom exactly - the kernel boots normally but the
display and USB gadget never come up (vendor modules built against the shipping
tree have mismatched __crc_ values, 125/282 for mali_kbase.ko), so the phone
looks dead while Android runs.

This hunk distinguishes the two: with -DDIAG_PANIC_AFTER_INIT the kernel panics
right after the last initcall, so

  * if a dump appears, the kernel finished initialising (the boot log in the
    dump then shows which driver probes failed -> display/USB), and
  * if no dump appears, the kernel really does die earlier, and the softlockup
    panic path gives the backtrace of the stuck CPU instead.

Only compiled in when KCFLAGS=-DDIAG_PANIC_AFTER_INIT is passed, so an ordinary
build of this tree is unaffected.

diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1052,6 +1052,16 @@ static int __ref kernel_init(void *unused)
 	numa_default_policy();
 
 	rcu_end_inkernel_boot();
 
+#ifdef DIAG_PANIC_AFTER_INIT
+	/* DIAG build only (KCFLAGS=-DDIAG_PANIC_AFTER_INIT): prove that the
+	 * kernel finished every initcall and hand the full boot log to SPRD
+	 * sysdump before userspace starts.  Used to tell a kernel that hangs
+	 * apart from a kernel that boots with dead display/USB.
+	 */
+	panic("DIAG: kernel init complete, about to exec init");
+#endif
 	pr_emerg("run init\n");
 	if (ramdisk_execute_command) {
 		ret = run_init_process(ramdisk_execute_command);
